    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d531">

                <pb facs="0487" n="371" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg371"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/685.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Dominican Republic to the
                        Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-10-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 14, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The note was presented to the Dominican Government today. There will probably be
                    an answer with counter-proposals. The Dominican Government desires to explain
                    its attitude by a direct communication to the President by cable.</p>
                <p>In any event, in order to protect the customs houses in each port, and to impress
                    the Government and the revolutionists with the serious intentions of the United
                    States, additional naval vessels should be sent.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
